  "replace_string": "<div class=\"mvu-helper-region\" data-mvu-helper=\"statusmenu\" data-mvu-helper-contract=\"move or hide this element whole - do not walk into it\">\n\n<!-- mvu-helper:begin statusmenu -->\n<!-- mvu-helper: this region is drawn by the mvu-helper extension. To move,\n     hide or skip it, match [data-mvu-helper] and take the whole element. Please do not infer our\n     boundary by walking the DOM - that is what this marker exists to spare you. -->\n\n<div style=\"border:1px dashed rgba(0,229,255,0.45);border-radius:8px;background:rgba(0,20,40,0.55);color:#e0f7fa;padding:14px 16px;line-height:1.5;font-size:0.9em;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;\">\n<h3 style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-size:1em;color:#00e5ff;letter-spacing:.02em;\">No menu built yet</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;\">This pack ships a PLACEHOLDER shell, so the pipeline works end to end and the dev loop\napplies without error - but there is no menu to draw.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;\">Design the real one in <b>MVU Status Menu Builder</b>, export the StatusMenu Pack, and drop\nits <code style=\"color:#81d4fa;\">regex/StatusMenu.json</code> over this one. It carries the same script name, so it\nreplaces this notice rather than sitting beside it.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;opacity:.75;font-size:.9em;\">Seeing this on a card whose pack DOES ship a menu means two regexes claim the\nplaceholder and this one is winning on list order - disable or delete it.</p>\n</div>\n\n<!-- mvu-helper:end statusmenu -->\n\n</div>",
